course: dictionary
lesson: 6727
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives each meaning its own number, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word oily can describe hands, fish, or a person, so the words around it are your best clue.
explain: «The takin's oily coat sheds rain and snow.» A coat that sheds rain has a coat covered with oil, so oily here means covered with oil or containing a lot of oil. Test it: put your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Oily can also describe a person. Imagine a shop assistant who says, «You look wonderful, you are so clever, I love your shoes!» every time you speak. If the praise seems too smooth and you feel you should not trust it, the word is oily in its third meaning: too polite and friendly in a way you do not trust.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, and the dictionary numbers them.
fact: Oily means covered with oil, like «oily hands», or containing a lot of oil, like «oily fish».
fact: Oily can also mean smooth and greasy, like «an oily liquid», or describe someone who is too polite in a way you do not trust.
fact: «Oily fish» like salmon and sardines are good for you, and oil does not mix with water: it floats on top.
fact: To choose the right meaning, read the sentence around the word and then swap in your meaning to check.
exercise: «The takin's oily coat sheds rain and snow.» What does oily mean here? | Too polite and friendly | Very cold to touch | Smooth and sticky like sugar | * Covered with oil, so water runs off
exercise: A person described as oily is... | Covered with mud | * Too polite and friendly in a way you do not trust | Very tall and thin | Full of sunshine
exercise: Which of these is an oily fish that is good for you? | Apple | * Salmon | Carrot | Bread
test: «Soap breaks apart the oily layer that sticks germs to the skin.» What does oily layer mean? | * Layer of grease, like oil | Layer of ice | Thin and see-through | Dry and dusty
test: In science, oil and water do not mix. What does oil do when you pour it on water? | Sinks to the bottom | * Floats on top | Mixes in evenly | Disappears
exam: Which sentence uses oily to mean too polite and friendly in a way you do not trust? | Skunks can spray a smelly liquid | The oil spill covered the beach | Soap is useful for washing your hands | * His oily compliments made me wary
